| PS1 || <math>L</math> is characteristic in <math>G</math> || (Char2) || (CS1), (CS5), (CS6) || -- || <toggledisplay><math>K</math> is characteristic in <math>G</math>, and <math>L/K = \Omega_1(Z(\overline{G}))</math> is characteristic in the quotient <math>\overline{G} = G/K</math>. Thus, by (Char2) (set: <math>A = K, I = L, B = G</math>), <math>L</math> is characteristic in <math>G</math>.</toggledisplay>
