| PS2 || <math>H</math> is characteristic in <math>G</math> || (Char5) || (CS1), (CS3) || -- || <toggledisplay>Since <math>H = C_G(K)</math>, we have, by (Char5) (set: <math>A = K, B = G</math>), that <math>H</math> is characteristic in <math>G</math>.</toggledisplay>
|-
| PS3 || <math>C</math> is characteristic in <math>G</math> || (Char4) || -- || (PS1), (PS2) || <toggledisplay>By (Char4), the subgroup <math>C = H \cap L</math> is characteristic in <math>G</math>.</toggledisplay>
